    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nKeep Qwen2-VL and Qwen3-VL video preprocessing from modifying a caller's list of frames.\n\nWhen a video is supplied as an odd-length list of images or image paths, `Qwen2VLPlugin._regularize_videos` pads it by appending the last frame directly to that list. Qwen3-VL inherits the same behavior. Reusing a five-frame video at 2 fps changes the final Qwen3-VL prompt timestamp from `<2.0 seconds>` on the first pass to `<2.2 seconds>` on the second; repeated supervised preprocessing also produces different input IDs. Copy the list before padding so its contents and subsequent timestamps stay stable.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The regression suite covers Qwen2-VL and Qwen3-VL with odd/even frame counts, PIL images and image paths. It also checks repeated Qwen3-VL prompt expansion and supervised preprocessing using a real Transformers video processor and a locally constructed tokenizer.\n- On unchanged upstream, the suite reports **6 failed, 4 passed**; with this change it reports **10 passed**.\n- Focused tests: Python 3.11 / Transformers 4.57.1, Python 3.12 / Transformers 5.8.0 and Python 3.13 / Transformers 5.8.0 each pass all 10 tests. Python 3.11 / Transformers 4.55.0 passes 8 and skips the 2 Qwen3-VL tests because its processor is unavailable.\n- Related processor, collator, formatter and converter tests on Python 3.13 / Transformers 5.8.0: **79 passed, 1 skipped**. The skip requires CPU or XPU; the local test runner selected MPS.\n- Ruff checks for the changed files, license checks, and offline source and wheel builds passed. The repository's CI-style formatting and quality sequence also passed in a disposable copy; it did not change either file in this PR.\n\nNo pretrained model weights or GPU training were used.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
